  "source_findings": [
    "Pbon is default R Holm, not Bonferroni or a paper-specific FDR policy. Complete nonmissing family is corrected before display filtering.",
    "Fewer than ten significant sets selects the first ten sorted rows, including nonsignificant sets and explicit all-NA padding beyond the source population.",
    "At least ten significant sets selects every strict adjusted-P<0.05 row; missing logical indices also yield explicit all-NA placeholder rows.",
    "Gene order/repeated IDs and first annotation match are retained. Missing/unmatched symbols stay NA, empty symbols stay empty; no fallback ID or normalization.",
    "Source accepts empty populations and negative/>1 P; native admission rejects those three cases explicitly. Original outputs remain retained.",
    "Declared GSA takes precedence; unused fallback is not consumed. Missing explicitly declared GSA fails rather than silently switching analysis. magma-skip3 requires three initial comment lines.",
    "Other fit fields are copied without certifying original models; raw formatting and exact original snapshots are retained."
  ],
  "scope": "Java-only supplied gene/set report postprocessing, no MAGMA fits/model certification, automatic fit bridge, historical biological-resource/whole-paper/full hosted FUMA/whole ROOT/release/deployment equivalence. Source numeric results measured with relative-only tolerance/exact zeros; source placeholders and stronger admission are explicit. FUMA remains missing,268 integrations and paper-wide audit remain open.",
  "proofs": {
